# The café over time (design/handson.md §6, §10, §11): jukebox records, seasons and the story
# calendar, decor themes, reward furniture, the station cat, polaroid journal captions, napkins,
# regulars' rituals. English placeholder texts in every language until T9 (see handson_TODO.txt).

# --- records (§10.2) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
record.rec_prague_swing.title
* Holešovice Swing, 1938

record.rec_prague_swing.artist
* The Tram Twelve Band — clarinet & brushes

record.rec_piano_trio.title
* Last Tram Trio

record.rec_piano_trio.artist
* Vltava Night Trio

record.rec_bossa_rain.title
* Bossa for a Rainy Platform

record.rec_bossa_rain.artist
* Lina Morais & friends

record.rec_folk_lullaby.title
* Kolyskova — Carpathian Lullabies

record.rec_folk_lullaby.artist
* bandura, cimbalom & accordion

record.rec_folk_lullaby.hint
* Someone from far away might bring one.

record.rec_folk_lullaby.source
* Oleh brought it from Lviv: "My grandmother's. It should play somewhere."

record.rec_synth_2039.title
* Holešovice 2039

record.rec_synth_2039.artist
* SLEEPER CAR

record.rec_synth_2039.hint
* A record that hasn't been made yet.

record.rec_synth_2039.source
* Filip cut it himself, in his room, at four in the morning.

record.rec_cafe_waltz.title
* Lida's Waltz

record.rec_cafe_waltz.artist
* a handwritten label: "Pro J."

record.rec_cafe_waltz.hint
* Grandma kept one record apart.

record.rec_cafe_waltz.source
* Found in an empty sleeve in the storeroom. The label says "Pro J." in grandma's hand.

record.rec_prague_swing.liked.mirek
* Ha! We danced to this at the depot party. 1987, I think.

record.rec_prague_swing.liked.radek
* Swing! The trams used to run on this rhythm.

record.rec_piano_trio.liked.radek
* Now that's music for a dispatcher. Everything on time.

record.rec_piano_trio.liked.guest_anwar
* …this one's nice to work to.

record.rec_bossa_rain.liked.lori
* Oh, that chord. Turn it up a little, would you?

record.rec_bossa_rain.disliked.mirek
* Too much samba for a Czech night, eh?

record.rec_folk_lullaby.liked.hana
* My mum sang that. I'd forgotten.

record.rec_folk_lullaby.liked.vera
* Hm. Lida used to hum this one. Badly.

record.rec_synth_2039.liked.filip
* Wait — is that my track? In here? I'm going to cry.

record.rec_synth_2039.liked.guest_anwar
* That's a good loop.

record.rec_synth_2039.disliked.vera
* That's not music, that's a fridge.

record.rec_cafe_waltz.liked.vera
* She played this every New Year's Eve. Every single one.

record.rec_cafe_waltz.liked.mirek
* …I haven't heard that in a long time, Karolina.

record.rec_cafe_waltz.liked.guest_333
* He hums along, very quietly.

