journal.empty
* night {night}

journal.keep
* Keep this one

journal.shake
* Shake it a little

journal.night
* Night {night}

journal.date
* {day} {month} {year}

journal.month.1
* Jan

journal.month.2
* Feb

journal.month.3
* Mar

journal.month.4
* Apr

journal.month.5
* May

journal.month.6
* Jun

journal.month.7
* Jul

journal.month.8
* Aug

journal.month.9
* Sep

journal.month.10
* Oct

journal.month.11
* Nov

journal.month.12
* Dec

journal.caption.guest_333
* 3:33. The clock stopped, and he was there again.

journal.caption.first_snow
* The first snow, through grandma's window.

journal.caption.mikulas
* An angel, a devil and three hot chocolates.

journal.caption.garlands_up
* Grandma's garlands, up again.

journal.caption.like_home
* It felt like home tonight.

journal.caption.perfect_serve
* {name} said it was exactly right.

journal.caption.cat_level
* The cat stayed. I think it lives here now.

journal.caption.full_house
* Every chair taken. Grandma would have loved it.

journal.caption.beautiful_latte
* A {pattern} for {name}.

journal.caption.record_loved
* {name} hummed along to {record}.

journal.caption.recipe_discovered
* My own recipe: {recipe}.

journal.caption.rozpis_happy
* Everyone got the nights they wanted.

journal.caption.anwar
* A quiet guy with a laptop. Nice smile.

journal.caption.quiet_night
* A quiet night. Rain on the window.

journal.caption.arc.mirek.1
* Mirek let me pour his coffee. Like he used to let her.

journal.caption.arc.mirek.2
* Mirek squinting at the menu board. "It's the letters, not my eyes."

journal.caption.arc.mirek.3
* Mirek came on foot tonight. He looked younger for it.

journal.caption.arc.mirek.4
* Twenty grams, and a whole life. Mirek finally told me.

journal.caption.arc.mirek.5
* Mirek, deciding. I didn't rush him.

journal.caption.arc.hana.1
* Hana laughed tonight: a baby girl called Lida.

journal.caption.arc.hana.2
* Hana asleep by the window. I let her be.

journal.caption.arc.hana.3
* Hana and her letter from Dresden.

journal.caption.arc.hana.4
* Hana decided. She looked lighter.

journal.caption.arc.guest_333.1
* Coins from 1979 on the saucer.

journal.caption.arc.guest_333.2
* "Still lit." He looked at the window, not at me.

journal.caption.arc.guest_333.3
* "I left once." The tea went cold in his hands.

journal.caption.arc.guest_333.4
* The last 3:33. The clocks started again.

journal.caption.arc.vera.1
* Vera and her crossword, recruiting the whole café.

journal.caption.arc.vera.2
* Vera inspected the table. It passed.

journal.caption.arc.vera.3
* Vera and grandma's kulajda. She closed her eyes on the first spoon.

journal.caption.arc.vera.4
* Vera's friends took over the corner. Loudly.

journal.caption.arc.filip.1
* Filip brought half his year to the socket table.

journal.caption.arc.filip.2
* Filip, very quiet, over a cold coffee.

journal.caption.arc.filip.3
* Filip before the resit. Fingers crossed, all of us.

journal.caption.arc.filip.4
* Filip got a B. The café cheered.

journal.caption.arc.radek.1
* Radek's warning came by text: the express is late. We were ready.

journal.caption.arc.radek.2
* Radek's last shift. He sat down for once.

journal.caption.arc.radek.3
* Radek and the snowdrifts of '85.

journal.caption.arc.lori.1
* Lori came in from the platform, guitar and all.

journal.caption.arc.lori.2
* Lori on the little stage. Almost a real one.

journal.caption.arc.lori.3
* Lori's Friday. The whole street listened.

journal.caption.scene.opening
* The first night. The keys were still cold.

journal.caption.scene.mirek_first
* Mirek, the very first regular.

journal.caption.scene.guest333_first
* 3:33. A man in an old coat ordered tea.

journal.caption.scene.vera_recipe
* Vera dictated, I wrote it down: kulajda.

journal.caption.scene.lori_platform
* Lori playing in the rain on platform two.

journal.caption.scene.hana_asleep
* Hana, finally asleep. The soup could wait.

journal.caption.scene.radek_last_shift
* The last whistle of Radek's career.

journal.caption.scene.lori_evening
* Lori's evening. Every chair, every window.

journal.caption.scene.filip_cake
* A cake for Filip, with one wonky candle.

journal.caption.scene.mirek_letter
* Mirek and the letter, at last.

journal.caption.scene.final_night
* The thirtieth night.

journal.caption.moment.m_blackout_candles
* The power went out. The candles didn't.

journal.caption.moment.m_lost_traveller
* A lost traveller, found. With three minutes to spare.

journal.caption.moment.m_sleeping_guest
* Someone asleep under grandma's blanket.

journal.caption.moment.m_coffee_for_helper
* A coffee for the crew, for once.

journal.caption.moment.m_busker
* A song under the awning, a tea in the rain.

journal.caption.moment.m_tired_parent
* Warm milk, and a little one asleep.

journal.caption.moment.m_advent_candle
* One more candle on the wreath.

# --- regulars' rituals (§6.3, SHOULD) ----------------------------------------------------------------------
ritual.mirek
* Mirek taps the counter twice.

ritual.vera
* Vera straightens the sugar bowl.

ritual.radek
* Radek checks his watch at the door.

ritual.hana
* Hana rubs her eyes.

ritual.filip
* Filip looks for a socket.

ritual.lori
* Lori shakes the rain off her raincoat.

ritual.guest_333
* The 3:33 guest looks at the window.

# --- thank-you napkins (§6.1, SHOULD) ------------------------------------------------------------------------
thanks.g01
* Thank you for the warm hands.

thanks.g02
* Best coffee between here and Adamov.

thanks.g03
* Caught my train! Thanks to you.

thanks.g04
* I came in sad. I'm leaving less sad.

thanks.g05
* The rain was nicer from your window.

thanks.g06
* You remembered I take it without sugar. Nobody remembers.

thanks.g07
* Same time tomorrow?

thanks.g08
* For the soup. And the quiet.

thanks.g09
* A good night after a bad day.

thanks.g10
* My shift was twelve hours. This made it eleven.

thanks.g11
* Say hi to the cat!

thanks.g12
* Thank you for not asking. And for the koláč.

thanks.g13
* Five stars. Six if the Wi-Fi worked.

thanks.g14
* I proposed here tonight. She said yes!

thanks.g15
* Next stop: home. Thank you for this one.

thanks.g16
* The best thing I tasted this year was at 3 a.m.

thanks.g17
* Drew this while waiting. Keep it.

thanks.g18
* You make strangers feel like regulars.

thanks.g19
* I'll tell my grandmother about your tea.

thanks.g20
* Stayed dry, stayed warm, stayed longer than I meant to.

thanks.g21
* The music was perfect. Who picks it?

thanks.g22
* That cup was exactly the right size of hug.

thanks.g23
* Night drivers' union says thanks.

thanks.g24
* The moon was out. So was your lamp.

thanks.g25
* A tip, and a secret: this is my favourite place.

thanks.g26
* The cat stole my napkin. This is the second one.

thanks.g27
* From the night ward, with tired love.

thanks.g28
* I'll be back when the snow comes.

thanks.g29
* Thank you for the window light. It helps, you know.

thanks.g30
* Stay open. Please.

thanks.mirek.1
* For the coffee. And for not asking. — M.

thanks.mirek.2
* She'd be proud. Don't make a fuss. — M.

thanks.hana.1
* You saved my night shift. Again. — H.

thanks.hana.2
* Twelve minutes of peace. Thank you. — H.

thanks.vera.1
* Acceptable. Very acceptable. — V. S.

thanks.vera.2
* The tea was proper. Tell nobody I said so. — V.

thanks.filip.1
* Passed! Partly your coffee's fault. — F.

thanks.radek.1
* The trains ran on time tonight. So did you. — R.

thanks.lori.1
* For the warm song you didn't know you sang. — L.

thanks.guest_333.1
* Děkuji.

